  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a user opening the app on 14 July, I want a short Bastille Day surprise — a statue-like bust of Marianne with fireworks around it and « Fête nationale » — so that the app celebrates the day without getting in my way.\n\nOperator request of 2026-10-28: « Première ouverture le 14/07 on affiche en overlay du forum un buste de Marianne (genre statue) et des feux d'artifice explose autour. Message « Fête nationale ». Animation 3 à 5sec max. » M4; first date 2027-07-14.\n\n### Blocked by\n\n- #256\n\n\n### Scope\n\n- First scene activation on 14/07 (local date), once per year: overlay over the forum list (any theme), 3–5 s, tap to dismiss, then gone; event state under a new `SettingKey` (`event.fete-nationale.<year>`).\n- Gated by « Animations de saison » (operator Q10) and Reduce Motion (then nothing plays); never over the keyboard, a sheet or the composer (THEMES.md §4); VoiceOver-silent except the « Fête nationale » text.\n- Uses LOT-166's overlay engine. Art: a generic statue-style bust (never the French government's « Marianne » logo) and fireworks in the charter of THEMES.md §6; drawing as on the reference boards in [`docs/assets/themes/`](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/tree/dev-swift/docs/assets/themes) (validated by the operator, 2026-11-10).\n\n### Legacy counterpart\n\nNone @ 87fe0d1c. New GAP row (gap-new, id = this issue), class `b·operator`.\n\n### Depends on\n\n- LOT-166 (#256)\n\n### Model\n\nSonnet 5.5 → Opus 5.5; Mac session for the art.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Injected calendar: 13/07 nothing, 14/07 first launch plays, second launch the same day nothing, 15/07 nothing, 14/07 the next year plays again; Reduce Motion and « Animations de saison » off: nothing.\n- [ ] Duration measured 3–5 s; dismissed by a tap.\n- [ ] `xcodebuild build test` green; checked on iPhone, iPad, Duo; strings in French; no new dependency; art credited.\n\n### Before you start (agents and humans)\n\nRead AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/THEMES.md §4–§5, the LOT-166 spec. Claim with `/claim <session-id>`; PR body `LOT-194`, `Closes #<this issue>`, `Claim: <session-id>`.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
